/* READING — Complete the Words (C-test) + Read in Daily Life
   diff : 2 = B2, 3 = C1, 4 = C2 (minimum B2) */
CONTENT.ctw = [
  { id: 'c01', diff: 2, topic: 'Biology', text: 'Bees play an essential role in the reproduction of many flowering plants. When a bee visits a flower to collect nectar, grains of pollen adhere to its body and are carried to the next blossom, where they fertilize the plant and allow it to produce seeds. Because so many crops depend on this process, the decline of bee populations, which scientists attribute to pesticides and habitat loss, could seriously reduce the global supply of fruit and vegetables.' },
  { id: 'c02', diff: 2, topic: 'Psychology', text: 'Sleep has a considerable influence on how effectively students learn. During the night, the brain consolidates the information it received during the day, transferring the most significant parts into permanent memory. Consequently, students who sacrifice sleep to study late before an examination often perform worse than those who rest properly. Many educators therefore recommend a regular sleep schedule, particularly during the most demanding periods of the academic year.' },
  { id: 'c03', diff: 2, topic: 'Economics', text: 'Inflation refers to a general rise in the prices of goods and services over time. When prices increase faster than wages, households can afford fewer products with the same amount of money. Central banks usually respond by raising interest rates, which makes borrowing more expensive and gradually reduces consumer spending. However, if rates rise too quickly, economic growth may slow down and unemployment can increase as a result.' },
  { id: 'c04', diff: 2, topic: 'Geology', text: 'Volcanoes form where molten rock from deep inside the Earth reaches the surface. Most of them are located along the edges of tectonic plates, which slowly move against or away from each other. When pressure builds up beneath the crust, gases and magma are forced upward through cracks in the rock. The resulting eruptions can destroy nearby towns, but they also create extremely fertile soil over time.' },
  { id: 'c05', diff: 3, topic: 'Finance', text: 'Diversification is one of the fundamental principles of modern portfolio management. By spreading capital across assets whose returns are not perfectly correlated, investors can reduce the overall volatility of their holdings without necessarily sacrificing expected performance. This insight, formalized in the nineteen fifties, transformed the way institutions allocate funds. Nevertheless, during severe financial crises, correlations between asset classes tend to increase sharply, which considerably limits the protection that diversification normally provides.' },
  { id: 'c06', diff: 2, topic: 'History', text: 'The invention of the printing press in the fifteenth century changed European society in profound ways. Before this innovation, books were copied by hand, which made them rare and extremely expensive. Once texts could be reproduced quickly, ideas began to circulate among a much larger public. Historians often argue that this development contributed to the spread of literacy and to major religious and scientific debates.' },
  { id: 'c07', diff: 3, topic: 'Neuroscience', text: 'Neuroplasticity describes the capacity of the brain to reorganize its structure in response to experience. Contrary to earlier assumptions, researchers have demonstrated that adult neurons can form new connections throughout life, particularly when individuals acquire complex skills such as a musical instrument or a foreign language. These findings have encouraged the development of rehabilitation programs for patients recovering from strokes, although the extent of possible recovery varies considerably between individuals.' },
  { id: 'c08', diff: 2, topic: 'Environment', text: 'Many cities are investing in the planting of trees along their streets. Trees provide shade in summer, which keeps buildings cooler and reduces the need for air conditioning. They also absorb pollutants from the air and offer a habitat for birds and insects. Several studies suggest that residents who live near green spaces experience less stress and are more inclined to exercise outdoors, which benefits public health as a whole.' },
  { id: 'c09', diff: 3, topic: 'Sociology', text: 'Urbanization has fundamentally altered patterns of social interaction across the globe. As populations concentrate in metropolitan areas, traditional networks based on kinship and proximity are frequently replaced by relationships formed through work, education, or shared interests. Some sociologists interpret this shift as a loss of community cohesion, while others emphasize the unprecedented freedom it offers individuals to construct their own identities. The debate remains unresolved, partly because empirical evidence points in both directions.' },
  { id: 'c10', diff: 2, topic: 'Marketing', text: 'Companies increasingly rely on data to understand the behavior of their customers. Every online purchase, search, or click leaves a trace that can be analyzed to predict future preferences. This information allows firms to design targeted advertisements that are more likely to convince potential buyers. At the same time, consumers and regulators have become more concerned about privacy, and new laws now limit how personal data may be collected.' },
  { id: 'c11', diff: 2, topic: 'Astronomy', text: 'The Moon does not produce any light of its own. What we see at night is sunlight reflected from its surface. As the Moon orbits the Earth, the proportion of its sunlit side that we can observe changes gradually, which explains why its apparent shape varies during the month. These regular cycles, known as phases, enabled ancient civilizations to organize their calendars and to plan their agricultural activities.' },
  { id: 'c12', diff: 3, topic: 'Linguistics', text: 'Bilingualism was once believed to confuse young children and delay their linguistic development. Contemporary research, however, suggests that individuals who regularly use two languages may develop stronger executive functions, including the ability to switch between tasks and to ignore irrelevant information. Critics point out that several of these studies failed to replicate, which has prompted researchers to adopt larger samples and more rigorous methods before drawing definitive conclusions.' },
  { id: 'c13', diff: 2, topic: 'Anthropology', text: 'Early human societies depended on hunting animals and gathering wild plants. Around twelve thousand years ago, some groups began to cultivate crops and domesticate animals in a process known as the agricultural revolution. Farming allowed people to produce more food in a smaller area, so populations grew and permanent villages appeared. However, early farmers often had a less varied diet than their hunting ancestors and suffered more frequently from infectious diseases.' },
  { id: 'c14', diff: 3, topic: 'Business', text: 'Corporate governance refers to the system of rules and practices through which a company is directed and controlled. A central concern is the potential conflict between shareholders, who own the firm, and managers, who run it on a daily basis. To align these interests, boards frequently link executive compensation to performance indicators measured over many years. Critics argue, however, that such incentives may push managers to take excessive risks when bonuses depend heavily on the share price in the near future.' },
  { id: 'c15', diff: 2, topic: 'Health', text: 'Drinking enough water is essential for good health. More than half of the human body consists of water, and a certain amount is lost every day through breathing, sweating, and other normal functions. When this loss is not replaced, people may experience fatigue, headaches, and difficulty concentrating. Doctors therefore advise adults to drink regularly throughout the day, especially in hot weather or during intense physical activity.' },
  { id: 'c16', diff: 2, topic: 'Architecture', text: 'Gothic cathedrals were designed to appear as tall and bright as possible. Builders in medieval Europe developed pointed arches and external supports called flying buttresses, which carried the weight of the roof away from the walls. Because the walls no longer had to support so much weight, architects could insert large windows of colored glass. The resulting interiors were filled with light, symbolizing the presence of the divine.' },
  { id: 'c17', diff: 3, topic: 'Ecology', text: 'Keystone species exert an influence on their ecosystems that is disproportionate to their abundance. The classic example is the sea otter, which preys on sea urchins along the Pacific coast. When otter populations declined because of hunting, urchins multiplied and consumed vast kelp forests, eliminating the habitat of numerous fish and invertebrates. Conservation efforts that restored the otters subsequently allowed these underwater forests to recover, illustrating how a single predator can shape an entire community.' },
  { id: 'c18', diff: 2, topic: 'Technology', text: 'Artificial intelligence systems learn by analyzing very large collections of examples. A program designed to recognize images, for instance, is shown millions of labeled pictures until it can identify common patterns on its own. The quality of the results therefore depends heavily on the data used during training. If the examples are incomplete or biased, the system may produce unfair or inaccurate decisions when it is applied in the real world.' },
  { id: 'c19', diff: 2, topic: 'Education', text: 'Many universities now offer a wide range of courses online. Students can watch lectures from home and progress at their own pace, which is particularly useful for people who work or live far from campus. However, some learners find it hard to stay motivated without regular contact with their classmates and teachers. For this reason, a growing number of programs combine online lessons with occasional meetings in small groups on campus.' },
  { id: 'c20', diff: 3, topic: 'Behavioral economics', text: 'Traditional economic models assume that individuals make rational decisions in order to maximize their own welfare. Behavioral economists have challenged this assumption by documenting systematic deviations from rationality, such as loss aversion, the tendency to weigh potential losses more heavily than equivalent gains. These insights have practical applications: governments increasingly design policies that gently nudge citizens toward beneficial choices, for example by automatically enrolling employees in retirement savings plans while preserving their freedom to opt out.' },
  { id: 'c21', diff: 2, topic: 'Chemistry', text: 'Water has several unusual properties that make life on Earth possible. Unlike most substances, it becomes less dense when it freezes, which is why ice floats on the surface of lakes and rivers. This layer of ice acts as insulation and keeps the water below from freezing completely during the winter. As a result, fish and other aquatic organisms are able to survive even in very cold climates.' },
  { id: 'c22', diff: 3, topic: 'Art history', text: 'Impressionism emerged in France during the second half of the nineteenth century as a reaction against the rigid conventions of academic painting. Rather than depicting historical or mythological scenes with meticulous precision, artists such as Monet sought to capture the fleeting effects of light and atmosphere on ordinary subjects. Critics initially ridiculed their loose brushwork and unfinished appearance, yet the movement eventually reshaped Western conceptions of what a painting could represent.' },
  { id: 'c23', diff: 2, topic: 'Transportation', text: 'Trains that travel at very high speeds have become a popular alternative to short flights in many countries. Although building new railway lines requires enormous investment, trains produce far less carbon dioxide per passenger than airplanes. They also take travelers directly to city centers, which saves time compared with reaching distant airports and passing through security checks. Consequently, several governments now encourage rail travel for journeys of less than four hours.' },
  { id: 'c24', diff: 2, topic: 'Zoology', text: 'Some species of birds travel thousands of kilometers every year. In autumn, they abandon cold regions where food becomes scarce and fly toward warmer climates. Scientists believe that these birds navigate by combining several cues, including the position of the Sun, the pattern of the stars, and the magnetic field of the Earth. Remarkably, many individuals return to exactly the same nest the following spring.' },
  { id: 'c25', diff: 3, topic: 'Political science', text: 'Democratic institutions depend not only on formal rules but also on informal norms of restraint. Constitutions rarely specify every circumstance in which power may be exercised, so political actors must voluntarily refrain from exploiting ambiguities for partisan advantage. When such norms erode, legal procedures may continue to operate while their underlying purpose is gradually undermined. Scholars therefore caution that democratic decline often occurs incrementally rather than through sudden and dramatic events.' },
  { id: 'c26', diff: 2, topic: 'Nutrition', text: 'Food labels are intended to help consumers make healthier choices. They indicate the amount of sugar, fat, and salt contained in a product, as well as its total energy value. Nevertheless, research shows that many shoppers rarely read this information carefully, especially when they are in a hurry. Some countries have therefore introduced simple color codes on packages so that buyers can compare products at a glance.' },
  { id: 'c27', diff: 3, topic: 'Accounting', text: 'Depreciation allows firms to allocate the cost of an asset that lasts for many years across the periods in which it generates revenue. Instead of recording the entire purchase price of a machine as an expense in the year of acquisition, the company spreads this amount over the estimated useful life of the equipment. This method provides a more accurate representation of profitability, although the choice of depreciation schedule inevitably involves assumptions that managers may be tempted to exploit.' },
  { id: 'c28', diff: 2, topic: 'Culture', text: 'Music is found in every known human culture. People sing to celebrate important events, to express grief, and to coordinate their efforts while working together. Parents all over the world sing soft lullabies to help their babies fall asleep. Some researchers speculate that music helped early humans to build cohesive groups by creating shared emotions and a sense of belonging, which would have improved their chances of survival.' },
  { id: 'c29', diff: 2, topic: 'Oceanography', text: 'The oceans absorb a large share of the heat and carbon dioxide produced by human activities. This process has slowed the warming of the atmosphere, but it also has serious consequences for marine life. As more carbon dioxide dissolves in seawater, the water becomes more acidic. This change makes it harder for corals and shellfish to build their protective structures, which threatens entire food chains.' },
  { id: 'c30', diff: 3, topic: 'Philosophy of science', text: 'According to Karl Popper, a theory qualifies as scientific only if it can, in principle, be falsified by empirical observation. This criterion was intended to distinguish genuine science from doctrines that accommodate every possible outcome and therefore explain nothing. Subsequent philosophers objected that scientists rarely abandon a theory after a single contradictory result, preferring instead to question auxiliary assumptions. Despite these objections, falsifiability remains an influential benchmark in debates about the boundaries of scientific inquiry.' },
];

CONTENT.dl = [
  { id: 'd01', diff: 2, label: 'Notice', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Posted at the entrance of Harper Library', title: 'Temporary Change to Opening Hours', body: '<p>Owing to the replacement of the flooring on the lower levels, Harper Library will close at <b>6 p.m.</b> rather than 11 p.m. from March 3 to March 14. Please note that the group study rooms on the second floor will remain unavailable throughout this period, as they are being used to store furniture.</p><p>Students who need a late-night study space are welcome to use the Science Center, which will stay open until midnight. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What is the reason for the change in opening hours?', o: ['Maintenance work on the building', 'A reduced number of students during exams', 'A shortage of library staff', 'The Science Center needs extra space'], a: 0, x: '« Owing to the replacement of the flooring » = à cause des travaux de remplacement des sols.' },
      { q: 'What can students do if they want to work after 6 p.m.?', o: ['Reserve a group study room in advance', 'Use the second floor of Harper Library', 'Ask the library staff for permission to stay', 'Go to the Science Center'], a: 3, x: 'Le Science Center reste ouvert jusqu\'à minuit ; les salles du 2e étage sont indisponibles.' },
      { q: 'Why are the group study rooms unavailable?', o: ['They are being repainted', 'They are reserved for exams', 'They are being converted into offices', 'They are being used to store furniture'], a: 3, x: '« they are being used to store furniture » = elles servent à entreposer du mobilier.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd02', diff: 2, label: 'Email', doc: { kind: 'email', from: 'Dr. Elena Ruiz', to: 'ECON 210 students', subject: 'Midterm review session', body: '<p>Hi everyone,</p><p>As several of you requested, I will hold an optional review session this Thursday from 4 to 6 p.m. in Room 118. I will go over the practice problems that caused the most difficulty, so please bring your graded problem sets.</p><p>If you can\'t make it, I\'ll post the slides afterward, but note that I won\'t be recording the session. Also, my regular office hours on Friday are cancelled this week.</p><p>Best,<br>Dr. Ruiz</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What is the main purpose of the email?', o: ['To announce a change in the exam date', 'To inform students about an extra review session', 'To remind students to submit their problem sets', 'To explain why office hours are important'], a: 1, x: 'Le cœur du message : une séance de révision optionnelle jeudi.' },
      { q: 'What should students bring to the session?', o: ['Their laptops', 'The slides', 'Their corrected problem sets', 'A list of questions'], a: 2, x: '« graded problem sets » = les exercices déjà corrigés/notés.' },
      { q: 'What can be inferred about students who miss the session?', o: ['They will not be able to watch a video of it', 'They can attend office hours on Friday', 'They will lose points on the midterm', 'They must email Dr. Ruiz'], a: 0, x: 'Elle ne l\'enregistre pas (« I won\'t be recording ») : pas de vidéo. Et les permanences de vendredi sont annulées.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd03', diff: 2, label: 'Text messages', doc: { kind: 'chat', head: 'Group chat — Flat 4B', msgs: [['Maya', 'Heads-up: the landlord is sending someone round at 10 tomorrow to sort out the heater. Can anyone be in?', '8:12 PM'], ['Tom', 'I\'d love to, but I\'ve got a lab session until noon 😕', '8:14 PM'], ['Leo', 'I can do it. I\'ll just push my shift back a couple of hours.', '8:20 PM'], ['Maya', 'You\'re a lifesaver! Could you also ask him to look at the radiator in my room? It keeps banging.', '8:21 PM'], ['Leo', 'Sure, no problem.', '8:22 PM']] },
    qs: [
      { q: 'Why is Tom unable to be at the flat?', o: ['He will be at a job interview', 'He is away for the week', 'He is waiting for a delivery', 'He has a class that lasts until midday'], a: 3, x: '« a lab session until noon » : il a TP jusqu\'à midi.' },
      { q: 'What does Maya mean when she writes "You\'re a lifesaver"?', o: ['She is very grateful to Leo', 'Leo has saved someone\'s life', 'She doubts that Leo can help', 'She is worried about Leo'], a: 0, x: 'Expression idiomatique de gratitude : « tu me sauves la mise ».' },
      { q: 'What additional request does Maya make?', o: ['To pay the landlord', 'To have the radiator in her room checked', 'To buy coffee for everyone', 'To change shifts with her'], a: 1, x: '« ask him to look at the radiator in my room » : faire examiner son radiateur.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd04', diff: 2, label: 'Advertisement', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Campus Recreation Center', title: 'Spring Climbing Workshop', body: '<p>Never climbed before? No problem! Our four-week beginner workshop covers safety techniques, knot-tying, and basic movement on the wall.</p><ul><li>Tuesdays, 7–9 p.m., starting April 2</li><li>$40 for students (equipment rental included)</li><li>Limited to 12 participants</li></ul><p>Participants who complete all four sessions will receive a belay certification, allowing them to use the wall independently during open hours. Register at the front desk — <b>spots fill up fast!</b></p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'Who is the workshop intended for?', o: ['People with no climbing experience', 'Instructors', 'Experienced climbers', 'Rec center employees'], a: 0, x: '« Never climbed before? No problem! » + « beginner workshop ».' },
      { q: 'What is required to obtain the certification?', o: ['Paying an extra fee', 'Passing a written test', 'Bringing personal equipment', 'Attending every session'], a: 3, x: '« complete all four sessions ».' },
      { q: 'What does the ad suggest about registration?', o: ['It can only be done online', 'It is free for students', 'Interested people should register early', 'It closes on April 2'], a: 2, x: '« spots fill up fast » + limité à 12 : il faut s\'inscrire vite.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd05', diff: 2, label: 'Menu', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Green Leaf Café — Lunch specials', title: 'Today\'s Menu', body: '<table><tr><td>Roasted tomato soup (vegan)</td><td>$4.50</td></tr><tr><td>Grilled chicken wrap with yogurt dressing</td><td>$7.00</td></tr><tr><td>Quinoa and roasted vegetable salad (vegan, gluten-free)</td><td>$6.50</td></tr><tr><td>Tuna melt on sourdough (contains gluten)</td><td>$6.00</td></tr></table><p class="small">Students receive 10% off on presentation of a valid ID. Refills on filter coffee are free until 11 a.m. Please inform staff of any allergies before ordering, as dishes may contain traces of nuts.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'Which dish would suit a customer who avoids both animal products and gluten?', o: ['Grilled chicken wrap', 'Tuna melt on sourdough', 'Roasted tomato soup', 'Quinoa and roasted vegetable salad'], a: 3, x: 'Seule la salade est indiquée à la fois « vegan » et « gluten-free » ; la soupe n\'est pas déclarée sans gluten.' },
      { q: 'What must a customer do to receive a reduction?', o: ['Show a student card', 'Buy a cup of coffee', 'Order before 11 a.m.', 'Order two dishes'], a: 0, x: '« 10% off on presentation of a valid ID » : réduction sur présentation de la carte étudiante.' },
      { q: 'What are customers with allergies asked to do?', o: ['Check the packaging of each dish', 'Tell the staff before ordering', 'Choose a vegan dish', 'Avoid the tuna melt'], a: 1, x: '« inform staff of any allergies before ordering ».' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd06', diff: 3, label: 'Email', doc: { kind: 'email', from: 'Housing Services', to: 'All residents, North Hall', subject: 'Water shut-off — action required', body: '<p>Dear residents,</p><p>Following the leak reported last week, contractors will replace a section of the main pipe on Wednesday. Water will be shut off building-wide from 9 a.m. to approximately 3 p.m.; however, delays cannot be ruled out.</p><p>Please make sure all taps are fully closed before 9 a.m. When service resumes, the water may appear cloudy for a few minutes; this is harmless, but we advise letting it run before drinking it. Residents with medical needs requiring running water should contact our office by Monday so that alternative arrangements can be made.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What is implied about the end of the shut-off?', o: ['It will definitely end at 3 p.m.', 'It depends on the residents', 'It will end earlier on Wednesday', 'It might last longer than planned'], a: 3, x: '« approximately » + « delays cannot be ruled out » = ça pourrait durer plus longtemps.' },
      { q: 'What are residents asked to do before the work begins?', o: ['Store drinking water', 'Leave the building', 'Close all their taps', 'Contact the contractors'], a: 2, x: '« make sure all taps are fully closed before 9 a.m. »' },
      { q: 'Why should some residents contact the office by Monday?', o: ['To arrange a solution for medical reasons', 'To request compensation', 'To complain about the leak', 'To volunteer to help the contractors'], a: 0, x: 'Pour ceux qui ont des besoins médicaux : « alternative arrangements ».' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd07', diff: 2, label: 'Social media post', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: '@UniDebateClub · 2h', body: '<p>Big news! 🎉 Our team made it to the national semi-finals for the first time in the club\'s history. Huge thanks to everyone who came to our practice rounds and gave feedback. We\'re now looking for volunteer judges for our next training weekend (Nov 16–17). No experience needed — we\'ll brief you. Pizza on us 🍕 DM us to sign up!</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What achievement does the post announce?', o: ['The club won the national championship', 'The team reached a stage of the competition it had never reached before', 'The club gained many new members', 'The club organized a national event'], a: 1, x: '« for the first time in the club\'s history » : première demi-finale.' },
      { q: 'What does the club offer volunteers?', o: ['Payment', 'Training to become debaters', 'Free food', 'A certificate'], a: 2, x: '« Pizza on us » = la pizza est offerte.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd08', diff: 2, label: 'Schedule', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Campus shuttle — Weekend timetable', title: 'Route B: Main Campus ↔ Train Station', body: '<table><tr><th>Leaves Main Campus</th><th>Arrives Station</th></tr><tr><td>8:00</td><td>8:25</td></tr><tr><td>10:30</td><td>10:55</td></tr><tr><td>13:00</td><td>13:25</td></tr><tr><td>17:30</td><td>17:55</td></tr></table><p class="small">The 13:00 departure does not run on Sundays. No service on public holidays. Bicycles are not permitted on board, but folding bikes may be carried if they are folded.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'A student on Saturday has a train at 18:10 and wants to reach the station at least ten minutes before it leaves. Which is the latest shuttle that would get her there in time?', o: ['8:00', '10:30', '13:00', '17:30'], a: 3, x: 'Le départ de 17:30 arrive à 17:55, soit 15 minutes avant le train de 18:10.' },
      { q: 'What can be inferred about Sunday service?', o: ['Only three shuttles leave Main Campus', 'The shuttle does not run at all', 'The journey takes longer than on Saturday', 'The last shuttle leaves at 13:00'], a: 0, x: 'Sans le départ de 13:00, il reste trois départs le dimanche.' },
      { q: 'Which of the following would NOT be allowed on board?', o: ['A full-size bicycle', 'A folded folding bike', 'A large suitcase', 'A backpack'], a: 0, x: 'Les vélos sont interdits, sauf les vélos pliants une fois pliés.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd09', diff: 3, label: 'Email', doc: { kind: 'email', from: 'Prof. James Okafor', to: 'Sofia Martin', subject: 'Re: Research assistant position', body: '<p>Dear Sofia,</p><p>Thank you for your interest in the position. Your background in statistics is certainly an asset, and I was impressed by your writing sample. That said, the project requires fieldwork in rural areas throughout July, and your message mentions an internship that overlaps with that period.</p><p>If your internship dates are flexible, I would be glad to discuss the role further. Otherwise, a smaller data-cleaning role may open in the autumn, and I would keep you in mind for it.</p><p>Kind regards,<br>James Okafor</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What is the professor\'s main concern?', o: ['Sofia lacks statistical skills', 'Sofia\'s writing sample was weak', 'Sofia may not be available during the fieldwork', 'The project has lost its funding'], a: 2, x: 'Le stage de Sofia chevauche le terrain de juillet.' },
      { q: 'What is the purpose of the phrase "That said" in the first paragraph?', o: ['To introduce a reservation', 'To add a compliment', 'To summarize the previous point', 'To give an example'], a: 0, x: '« That said » = « cela dit » : introduit une restriction après des compliments.' },
      { q: 'What does the professor offer if Sofia cannot change her plans?', o: ['A paid internship', 'A meeting in July', 'A recommendation letter', 'A possible role later in the year'], a: 3, x: 'Un rôle de nettoyage de données pourrait ouvrir à l\'automne.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd10', diff: 2, label: 'Notice', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Laundry room, Building C', title: 'PLEASE READ', body: '<p>Machines 3 and 4 are out of order. A technician has been called.</p><p>Remember: clothes left in machines for more than 30 minutes after the cycle ends may be removed and placed on the shelf. The building is not responsible for lost items.</p><p>Card top-up machine now accepts contactless payment.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What will happen to clothes left in a machine too long?', o: ['They will be thrown away', 'They may be moved to a shelf', 'They will be taken to lost and found', 'The owner will be fined'], a: 1, x: '« may be removed and placed on the shelf ».' },
      { q: 'What change is mentioned about payment?', o: ['Cards can now be recharged with contactless payment', 'Prices have increased', 'Cash is no longer accepted', 'Machines 3 and 4 are now free'], a: 0, x: 'La borne de recharge accepte désormais le sans contact.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd11', diff: 2, label: 'Text messages', doc: { kind: 'chat', head: 'Messages', msgs: [['Alex', 'Ugh, my bus has broken down and the next one isn\'t for twenty minutes. I\'m going to be late. Can you save me a seat? 🙄', '6:47 PM'], ['Priya', 'Of course. They\'re still showing trailers, so you won\'t miss anything. Shall I grab you some popcorn?', '6:49 PM'], ['Alex', 'You\'re a star, thanks! I\'ll text you as soon as I\'m outside.', '6:50 PM']] },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What has caused Alex\'s delay?', o: ['He misjudged the time', 'He took the wrong route', 'His bus has had a breakdown', 'He had to wait for a friend'], a: 2, x: '« my bus has broken down » : le bus est tombé en panne.' },
      { q: 'What can be inferred about the film?', o: ['It started twenty minutes ago', 'It is being shown twice', 'It has been cancelled', 'It has not started yet'], a: 3, x: '« They\'re still showing trailers » : la bande-annonce passe encore, le film n\'a pas commencé.' },
      { q: 'What does Priya offer to do?', o: ['Wait for Alex outside the cinema', 'Buy a snack for Alex', 'Order a taxi for Alex', 'Pay for Alex\'s ticket'], a: 1, x: '« Shall I grab you some popcorn? » : elle propose de lui prendre du pop-corn.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd12', diff: 3, label: 'Policy excerpt', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Student Handbook, Section 4.2', title: 'Late Submission Policy', body: '<p>Assignments submitted after the deadline will incur a penalty of 5% per calendar day, up to a maximum of seven days, after which a grade of zero will be recorded. Extensions may be granted only in cases of documented illness or exceptional circumstances, and requests must be submitted <i>before</i> the original deadline, except where the nature of the emergency makes this impossible. Technical problems, such as computer failure, do not constitute grounds for an extension.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'A student submits an essay three days late without an extension. What happens?', o: ['The essay receives zero', 'The essay is not accepted', 'The grade is reduced by 5%', 'The grade is reduced by 15%'], a: 3, x: '5 % par jour × 3 jours = 15 %.' },
      { q: 'According to the policy, which situation would most likely NOT justify an extension?', o: ['A laptop that stopped working', 'A family emergency', 'A hospital stay', 'A serious illness with a doctor\'s note'], a: 0, x: '« Technical problems, such as computer failure, do not constitute grounds ».' },
      { q: 'The word "incur" in the text is closest in meaning to', o: ['avoid', 'receive', 'calculate', 'cancel'], a: 1, x: '« incur a penalty » = subir/recevoir une pénalité.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd13', diff: 2, label: 'Email', doc: { kind: 'email', from: 'Career Center', to: 'Final-year students', subject: 'Mock interviews with alumni', body: '<p>Hello,</p><p>Next week, alumni working in finance, consulting and tech will be on campus to run 20-minute mock interviews. Each student may book <b>one</b> slot through the Career Portal. Sessions are conducted in English, and you will receive written feedback within 48 hours.</p><p>We strongly recommend uploading your CV beforehand so that interviewers can tailor their questions. Slots are allocated on a first-come, first-served basis.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What is the maximum number of interviews a student can book?', o: ['One', 'Two', 'Three', 'Unlimited'], a: 0, x: '« may book one slot ».' },
      { q: 'Why are students advised to upload their CV?', o: ['It is required to book a slot', 'To receive feedback faster', 'To be sent to employers', 'So that questions can be adapted to them'], a: 3, x: '« so that interviewers can tailor their questions » = adapter.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd14', diff: 2, label: 'Sign', doc: { kind: 'notice', title: '⚠ Wet Paint — Please Do Not Sit', body: '<p>The benches in this area were repainted this morning, and the paint will not be fully dry until Friday. We kindly ask you to refrain from sitting on them until then. If you accidentally touch the paint, please inform our office so that we can advise you on how to remove it.</p><p>Thank you for your understanding. — Grounds Maintenance</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What are people being asked to do?', o: ['Clean the benches after use', 'Report any damage to the benches', 'Help to repaint the benches', 'Stay off the benches for a few days'], a: 3, x: 'Ne pas s\'asseoir avant vendredi, le temps que la peinture sèche.' },
      { q: 'What should someone do if they touch the paint?', o: ['Inform Grounds Maintenance', 'Wait until Friday', 'Wash the bench', 'Nothing in particular'], a: 0, x: '« please inform our office » : prévenir le service d\'entretien.' },
      { q: 'In the sign, "refrain from" is closest in meaning to', o: ['avoid doing', 'continue doing', 'begin doing', 'be forced to do'], a: 0, x: '« refrain from sitting » = s\'abstenir de s\'asseoir.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd15', diff: 3, label: 'Online review', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Review of "Casa Verde" · ★★★☆☆', body: '<p>I had high hopes after all the hype, and the food certainly lived up to it — the mushroom risotto was outstanding. Unfortunately, the service left a lot to be desired: we waited nearly forty minutes for our mains, and our server seemed to forget us twice. I\'d go back for the food, but only on a quiet weekday.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What is the reviewer\'s overall opinion?', o: ['Everything was excellent', 'The food was good but the service was poor', 'The restaurant was too quiet', 'The food was disappointing'], a: 1, x: 'Nourriture « outstanding », service « left a lot to be desired ».' },
      { q: 'What does "lived up to it" mean in context?', o: ['Was as good as expected', 'Was too expensive', 'Was served quickly', 'Was better on weekdays'], a: 0, x: '« live up to the hype » = être à la hauteur des attentes.' },
      { q: 'Why would the reviewer return only on a quiet weekday?', o: ['Prices are lower then', 'The menu is different', 'Service might be better when it is less busy', 'The risotto is only served then'], a: 2, x: 'Inférence : moins de monde → meilleur service.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd16', diff: 2, label: 'Form', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Room Booking Confirmation', body: '<p><b>Room:</b> Seminar Room 2.14 &nbsp; <b>Date:</b> Tue 12 Nov &nbsp; <b>Time:</b> 14:00–16:00</p><p><b>Booked by:</b> Investment Society</p><p><b>Equipment:</b> projector ✔ &nbsp; microphone ✘ &nbsp; video-conference ✔</p><p class="small">Cancellations must be made at least 24 hours in advance. No-shows may lose booking privileges for the rest of the term.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'Which equipment will NOT be available?', o: ['A projector', 'Chairs', 'Video-conference equipment', 'A microphone'], a: 3, x: 'microphone ✘.' },
      { q: 'What could happen if the society does not use the room and does not cancel?', o: ['They will pay a fine', 'They may be unable to book rooms for the term', 'They will be moved to another room', 'Nothing'], a: 1, x: '« may lose booking privileges for the rest of the term ».' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd17', diff: 2, label: 'Email', doc: { kind: 'email', from: 'Sam', to: 'Julia', subject: 'Notes from today', body: '<p>Hi Julia,</p><p>I was sorry to hear you were ill today. I\'ve attached my notes from the biology lecture, though I\'m afraid they\'re a bit messy, so let me know if anything isn\'t clear. The professor also mentioned that the quiz has been put off until next Monday, which should give you plenty of time to catch up. Hope you\'re feeling better soon!</p><p>Sam</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'Why is Sam writing to Julia?', o: ['To apologize for missing a lecture', 'To offer help with the lecture she missed', 'To ask to borrow her notes', 'To invite her to a study group'], a: 1, x: 'Il envoie ses notes du cours manqué et propose de clarifier au besoin.' },
      { q: 'What does Sam say about the notes?', o: ['They are incomplete', 'They were taken by someone else', 'They were written by the professor', 'They may be hard to follow'], a: 3, x: '« a bit messy, so let me know if anything isn\'t clear » : elles sont un peu brouillonnes.' },
      { q: 'In the email, "put off until" is closest in meaning to', o: ['postponed until', 'repeated', 'cancelled', 'shortened to'], a: 0, x: '« put off » = repousser, reporter.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd18', diff: 3, label: 'Announcement', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Office of the Provost', title: 'Pilot: Pass/Fail Option for Electives', body: '<p>Beginning next semester, undergraduates may elect to take <b>one</b> elective per term on a pass/fail basis. Courses required for a student\'s major or minor are excluded. The decision must be declared by the end of the fourth week and is irreversible thereafter.</p><p>While a "pass" will count toward graduation credits, it will not be factored into the grade point average. Students intending to apply to graduate programs are encouraged to consult an advisor, as some programs view pass/fail grades less favorably.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'Which course could a student take pass/fail?', o: ['A required course in their major', 'Any course, without limit', 'One optional course outside their major requirements', 'Only courses in their minor'], a: 2, x: 'Un seul cours optionnel ; majeure et mineure exclues.' },
      { q: 'What does "irreversible thereafter" imply?', o: ['Students can change their decision at any time', 'After week four, the choice cannot be changed', 'The policy will be reversed next year', 'Students must declare before the semester starts'], a: 1, x: '« thereafter » = après cette date ; « irreversible » = définitif.' },
      { q: 'Why are some students advised to see an advisor?', o: ['Pass/fail courses cost more', 'Advisors must approve every elective', 'The option lowers the GPA', 'Some graduate programs may judge these grades negatively'], a: 3, x: '« some programs view pass/fail grades less favorably ».' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd19', diff: 2, label: 'Text messages', doc: { kind: 'chat', head: 'Project group', msgs: [['Nina', 'Can we push the meeting to 5? My seminar runs over on Wednesdays.', '10:02'], ['Omar', 'Works for me. I\'ll book the same room.', '10:05'], ['Chloé', 'I have to leave at 5:30 so I can only join for the first half hour. I\'ll send my slides tonight.', '10:11']] },
    qs: [
      { q: 'Why does Nina want to change the meeting time?', o: ['She has a job interview', 'Her seminar usually finishes late', 'The room is not available', 'She prefers mornings'], a: 1, x: '« runs over » = déborde, finit en retard.' },
      { q: 'What will Chloé do?', o: ['Miss the meeting completely', 'Present the slides at the meeting', 'Book the room', 'Attend part of the meeting and share her slides in advance'], a: 3, x: 'Elle ne peut venir qu\'une demi-heure et enverra ses slides ce soir.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd20', diff: 2, label: 'Poster', doc: { kind: 'notice', title: 'Lost: Black Backpack', body: '<p>I left my black backpack in the main cafeteria on Monday around lunchtime. It contains a laptop and a red notebook with the only copy of my thesis notes, so it means a great deal to me. No questions asked, and there is a reward for its safe return. If you have seen it, please call or text Daniel on 555-0142.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'Why is the notebook so important to Daniel?', o: ['It was an expensive gift', 'It holds the only copy of his research notes', 'It contains his contact details', 'It has his laptop password'], a: 1, x: '« the only copy of my thesis notes » : l\'unique exemplaire de ses notes de thèse.' },
      { q: 'What does Daniel promise to anyone who returns the backpack?', o: ['A reward and no further questions', 'A replacement laptop', 'Lunch at the cafeteria', 'A copy of his thesis'], a: 0, x: '« No questions asked » + « a reward ».' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd21', diff: 3, label: 'Email', doc: { kind: 'email', from: 'Dr. Lin Zhao', to: 'Thesis supervisees', subject: 'Draft chapters — revised timeline', body: '<p>Dear all,</p><p>Having now read the first round of drafts, I am revising our timeline. Rather than submitting a full second chapter by the 15th, please send me a detailed outline together with a two-page sample of your analysis. This will allow us to identify structural issues before you invest weeks in writing.</p><p>Those whose methodology still needs approval from the ethics committee should prioritize that application, as delays at that stage have held up several projects in previous years.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'Why is Dr. Zhao changing the timeline?', o: ['Students are behind schedule', 'She will be away on the 15th', 'She wants to catch structural problems early', 'The ethics committee requested it'], a: 2, x: '« identify structural issues before you invest weeks in writing ».' },
      { q: 'What must students now submit by the 15th?', o: ['A complete second chapter', 'Revised first chapters', 'Their ethics application', 'An outline and a short sample'], a: 3, x: '« a detailed outline together with a two-page sample ».' },
      { q: 'What can be inferred about ethics approval?', o: ['It is usually quick', 'It has caused delays in the past', 'It is not required for most students', 'Dr. Zhao handles it herself'], a: 1, x: '« delays at that stage have held up several projects in previous years ».' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd22', diff: 2, label: 'Receipt', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'CITY BOOKS — Receipt #20481', body: '<table><tr><td>Principles of Corporate Finance (used)</td><td>$62.00</td></tr><tr><td>Graph paper notebook ×2</td><td>$7.00</td></tr><tr><td>Student discount (10% on books only)</td><td>−$6.20</td></tr><tr><td><b>Total</b></td><td><b>$62.80</b></td></tr></table><p class="small">Returns accepted within 14 days with receipt. Used books: exchange only, no refunds.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What did the discount apply to?', o: ['The whole purchase', 'The notebooks only', 'The textbook only', 'Nothing'], a: 2, x: '« 10% on books only » : 10 % de 62 $ = 6,20 $.' },
      { q: 'If the customer wants to return the textbook next week, what can they get?', o: ['A full refund', 'A partial refund', 'Only an exchange', 'Nothing, returns are not accepted'], a: 2, x: 'Livre d\'occasion : « exchange only, no refunds ».' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd23', diff: 2, label: 'Notice', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Gym — Front desk', title: 'Towel Service', body: '<p>As of Monday, towels will no longer be supplied free of charge. Members may either bring their own or hire one at the front desk for $1 per visit. This change is part of our effort to cut down on water and detergent consumption, and the savings will be invested in new equipment for the weights room.</p><p>Premium members will continue to receive complimentary towels.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What is changing at the gym?', o: ['Most members will have to pay for towels', 'The gym will close on Mondays', 'Members must wash their own towels', 'Premium membership will be abolished'], a: 0, x: 'Les serviettes ne sont plus gratuites (1 $) sauf pour les membres premium.' },
      { q: 'What will the money saved be used for?', o: ['Lowering membership fees', 'Paying the water bills', 'Hiring more staff', 'Buying new equipment'], a: 3, x: '« invested in new equipment for the weights room ».' },
      { q: 'Who will still get free towels?', o: ['Premium members', 'New members', 'Students', 'Anyone who arrives early'], a: 0, x: '« Premium members will continue to receive complimentary towels ». « complimentary » = gratuit.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd24', diff: 3, label: 'Forum post', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Forum › Graduate admissions › "Is the GMAT still worth it?"', body: '<p><b>finance_hopeful:</b> Everyone keeps saying test-optional is the new normal, but from what I\'ve gathered, the top programs still expect a strong score from applicants without a quantitative background. If your undergrad transcript already shows advanced math, you can probably get away with skipping it. Otherwise, I\'d bite the bullet and take it — it\'s a signal admissions committees still read.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What is the writer\'s main point?', o: ['The GMAT is no longer important', 'Everyone should skip the GMAT', 'The GMAT is still useful for applicants lacking quantitative evidence', 'Top programs have abolished the test'], a: 2, x: 'Utile si le dossier ne montre pas déjà un bon niveau quantitatif.' },
      { q: 'What does "bite the bullet" mean here?', o: ['Give up', 'Do something difficult but necessary', 'Take a risk with money', 'Complain loudly'], a: 1, x: 'Idiome : se résoudre à faire quelque chose de désagréable mais nécessaire.' },
      { q: 'The phrase "get away with" suggests that skipping the test would be', o: ['acceptable without negative consequences', 'illegal', 'strongly recommended', 'impossible'], a: 0, x: '« get away with » = s\'en tirer sans conséquence.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd25', diff: 2, label: 'Email', doc: { kind: 'email', from: 'IT Help Desk', to: 'All users', subject: 'Scheduled maintenance Saturday', body: '<p>The university email system will be unavailable on Saturday between 1 and 5 a.m. for a security upgrade. After the upgrade, all users will be required to set up two-step verification the next time they sign in. Instructions are available on the IT website. We recommend doing this from a computer rather than a phone.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What will users need to do after the upgrade?', o: ['Change their password', 'Install new software', 'Activate an extra security step when logging in', 'Contact the help desk'], a: 2, x: '« set up two-step verification ».' },
      { q: 'Why was the maintenance probably scheduled between 1 and 5 a.m.?', o: ['Staff are cheaper at night', 'The upgrade takes exactly four hours', 'It is required by law', 'Few people use email then'], a: 3, x: 'Inférence : minimiser la gêne pour les utilisateurs.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd26', diff: 2, label: 'Invitation', doc: { kind: 'notice', title: 'International Food Night 🌍', body: '<p>Join us on Friday at 7 p.m. in the Student Union Hall for a celebration of the many cultures represented on campus. Bring a dish from your home country to share and you will get in free; everyone else pays $5 at the door. There will be live music, board games from around the world and a prize for the most original recipe. Please label your dish with its main ingredients so that guests with allergies can choose safely.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'How can a guest avoid paying the entrance fee?', o: ['By arriving early', 'By volunteering', 'By helping to set up', 'By contributing a dish'], a: 3, x: '« Bring a dish ... and you will get in free ».' },
      { q: 'Why are guests asked to label their dishes?', o: ['So that a prize can be awarded', 'So that dishes can be returned afterwards', 'So that guests with allergies can choose safely', 'So that dishes can be sorted by country'], a: 2, x: '« so that guests with allergies can choose safely ».' },
      { q: 'What is the main aim of the event?', o: ['To celebrate the cultural diversity of the campus', 'To raise funds for charity', 'To train future cooks', 'To introduce new professors'], a: 0, x: '« a celebration of the many cultures represented on campus ».' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd27', diff: 3, label: 'Memo', doc: { kind: 'email', from: 'Head of Department', to: 'Teaching assistants', subject: 'Grading consistency', body: '<p>Colleagues,</p><p>A review of last term\'s marks revealed notable discrepancies between sections of the same course, with average grades differing by nearly a full letter. To address this, each TA will independently grade a common set of five anonymized essays next week, after which we will meet to calibrate our use of the rubric.</p><p>This is not an evaluation of individual TAs; rather, it is intended to ensure students are assessed fairly regardless of their section.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What problem does the memo identify?', o: ['TAs graded too slowly', 'Grades varied too much between sections', 'Students complained about essays', 'The rubric was lost'], a: 1, x: '« notable discrepancies between sections ».' },
      { q: 'Why does the writer include the final paragraph?', o: ['To announce a penalty', 'To explain the rubric', 'To ask TAs for feedback', 'To reassure TAs that they are not being judged'], a: 3, x: '« This is not an evaluation of individual TAs » : rassurer.' },
      { q: 'The word "calibrate" is closest in meaning to', o: ['adjust to a common standard', 'measure the length of', 'criticize', 'simplify'], a: 0, x: 'Calibrer = harmoniser sur une même référence.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd28', diff: 2, label: 'Text messages', doc: { kind: 'chat', head: 'Messages', msgs: [['Ben', 'Did you manage to get tickets for the career fair talk?', '09:15'], ['Lucie', 'Sold out by the time I logged in 😩 But they\'re streaming it live.', '09:17'], ['Ben', 'Better than nothing. Want to watch it together in the library?', '09:18'], ['Lucie', 'Deal. Room 3 has a big screen.', '09:18']] },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What problem did Lucie have?', o: ['She forgot her password', 'There were no tickets left', 'The talk was cancelled', 'The library was closed'], a: 1, x: '« Sold out » = complet.' },
      { q: 'What will they probably do?', o: ['Attend the talk in person', 'Buy tickets for another talk', 'Skip the talk', 'Watch the talk online together'], a: 3, x: 'Streaming dans la salle 3 de la bibliothèque. « Deal » = d\'accord.' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd29', diff: 2, label: 'Notice', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Chemistry Department', title: 'Lab Safety Reminder', body: '<p>Goggles and closed-toe shoes are mandatory at all times in Labs 1–4. Students who arrive without proper footwear will not be admitted and the session will count as an unexcused absence. Spare goggles can be borrowed from the technician\'s office, but shoes cannot.</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What happens if a student wears sandals to the lab?', o: ['They can borrow shoes', 'They will be refused entry and marked absent', 'They must sign a form', 'They will receive a warning only'], a: 1, x: 'Pas admis + absence non justifiée.' },
      { q: 'What can students borrow?', o: ['Shoes', 'Lab coats', 'Protective glasses', 'Gloves'], a: 2, x: '« Spare goggles can be borrowed ».' },
    ] },
  { id: 'd30', diff: 3, label: 'Newsletter excerpt', doc: { kind: 'notice', head: 'Business School Newsletter — Faculty spotlight', body: '<p>Professor Adeyemi\'s latest paper challenges the conventional wisdom that remote work inevitably erodes productivity. Drawing on data from over 2,000 employees, she finds that output held steady overall, but that junior staff received markedly less informal mentoring. "The cost isn\'t in the spreadsheet," she notes, "it\'s in the careers of people who never got to overhear how decisions are made."</p>' },
    qs: [
      { q: 'What does the study conclude about productivity?', o: ['It fell sharply', 'It could not be measured', 'It increased among junior staff', 'It remained stable overall'], a: 3, x: '« output held steady overall ».' },
      { q: 'What does Professor Adeyemi mean by "The cost isn\'t in the spreadsheet"?', o: ['Remote work is financially expensive', 'The main disadvantage is hard to measure in numbers', 'Companies hide their costs', 'Her data were incomplete'], a: 1, x: 'Le coût (moins de mentorat) n\'apparaît pas dans les chiffres de productivité.' },
      { q: 'Who is most affected by remote work, according to the study?', o: ['Senior managers', 'Clients', 'Researchers', 'Junior employees'], a: 3, x: '« junior staff received markedly less informal mentoring ».' },
    ] },
];
